# Vite loads env files by mode — see https://vite.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html
#
# - `.env.development` is committed and already points at local Supabase
#   (`supabase start`); `npm run dev` uses it automatically, zero setup needed.
# - For production, copy this file to `.env.production` (gitignored — never
#   commit it) and fill in the values from your Supabase project
#   (Dashboard → Project Settings → API). Only the anon/publishable key
#   belongs here — NEVER the service_role key: everything in this file is
#   shipped to the browser. Row Level Security is what protects per-user data.
# - For staging (a second, disposable hosted project used to rehearse
#   migrations before production), copy this file to `.env.staging`
#   (also gitignored) instead. `npm run dev:staging` / `vite build --mode
#   staging` read it. See docs/RUNBOOK.md §5 for the staging → production flow.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# `local` | `staging` | `production` — drives the non-production banner
# (src/app/EnvBanner.tsx). Set to exactly `production` to hide it; anything
# else (including unset) shows it, fail-safe.
VITE_ENV_LABEL=
# Optional. Sentry DSN (Project Settings → Client Keys) for client-side error
# reporting (src/lib/sentry.ts). Leave unset to disable reporting entirely —
# init() is a no-op without it, so local/dev is silent by default.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
